  publication: THE GRAYFORD GAZETTE
  publicationDate: November 14, 1991
  headline: Mercer Inquiry Sees No New Developments
  articleBody: "Nearly four weeks after Daniel Mercer's disappearance, the sheriff's office reports no significant developments in the inquiry.\n\n      Officials continue to regard voluntary departure as the most likely explanation. A department representative declined to comment on the specific information supporting that assessment.\n\n      Mercer's family has expressed frustration with the lack of answers. No publicly confirmed account of his departure has emerged.\n\n      The Gazette will report further developments as information becomes available."
  evidenceID: gazette_followup_report
  evidenceTitle: Gazette Follow-up
  journalNote: The follow-up repeated the departure account but cited no witness who saw Daniel leave Grayford.
